Requirements: 6   with obligations: 6

[task-01] When the benchmark's instability measurement finishes, it prints the per-stage
    usage table that `acceptance check` and `acceptance decompose` already print,
    covering every model call the measurement made, with live and replayed calls counted
    apart.
    -> instability-measurement-prints-usage-table  [functional/explicit, code_and_tests]
       When the benchmark's instability measurement finishes, it prints the same per-
       stage usage table that `acceptance check` and `acceptance decompose` already
       print.
    -> usage-table-covers-every-measurement-call  [functional/explicit, code_and_tests]
       The per-stage usage table printed when the benchmark's instability measurement
       finishes accounts for every model call the measurement made, so that the table's
       totals equal the number of model calls issued during the measurement, with none
       omitted.
    -> usage-table-live-replayed-counted-apart  [functional/explicit, code_and_tests]
       The per-stage usage table printed at the end of the benchmark's instability
       measurement reports live model calls and replayed model calls as separate counts,
       rather than as a single combined figure.

[task-02] The table shows what the run spent on Claude models separately from what it
    spent on any other provider, so the Claude credits a run consumed can be read off as
    a figure of its own. A call sent through the Message Batches API counts at the price
    it was billed at.
    -> claude-spend-separate-figure  [functional/explicit, code_and_tests]
       The table presents the run's spend on Claude models as a figure separate from the
       run's spend on any other provider, so the Claude credits consumed by a run can be
       read off as its own figure.
    -> batch-call-counted-at-billed-price  [functional/explicit, code_and_tests]
       A call sent through the Message Batches API is counted in the run's spend at the
       price it was billed at (the batch price), not at the standard non-batch price for
       the same model.

